<title>DENMARK: CYCLING-DENMARK TOUR STAGE THREE PLACING/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-DENMARK TOUR STAGE THREE PLACING/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading placings and overall</p>
<p>standings after the 120 km third stage of the Tour of Denmark</p>
<p>cycling race between Nordborg and Haderslev, southwest Denmark</p>
<p>on Friday:</p>
<p>1. Christian Henn (Germany) Telekom two hours 37 mins 28 secs</p>
<p>2. Michael Skelde (Denmark) Post Danmark 2 seconds behind</p>
<p>3. Juris Silvos (Latvia) Oeschelbronn 11 seconds behind</p>
<p>4. Bo Hamburger (Denmark) TVM same time as Silvos</p>
<p>5. Brian Holm (Denmark) Telekom 14 seconds behind</p>
<p>6. Michael Kyneb (Denmark) Post Danmark</p>
<p>7. Fabrizio Guidi (Italy) Scrigno</p>
<p>8. Jan Schaffrath (Germany) Telekom</p>
<p>9. Bjarne Riis (Denmark) Telekom</p>
<p>10.Peter Meinert (Denmark) US Postal all same time as Holm</p>
<p>Overall standings (after threee stages)</p>
<p>1. Giovanni Lombardi (Italy) Telekom 10 hours 22 mins 55 secs</p>
<p>2. Fabrizio Guidi three seconds behind</p>
<p>3  Robbie McEwen (Australia) Rabobank same time</p>
<p>4. Christian Henn five seconds behind</p>
<p>5  Juris Silvos 11 seconds behind</p>
<p>6. Bo Hamburger 16 seconds behind</p>
<p>7. Peter Meinert same time</p>
<p>8. Leon Van Bon (Netherlands) Rabobank 18 seconds behind</p>
<p>9. Bjarne Riis 19 seconds behind</p>
<p>10. Adriano Baffi (Italy) US Postal 20 seconds behind</p>
</text>
